-- title:
--   Global element of reduced norm q normalising the completed orders
-- statement:
--   Fix $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$, a prime $q\neq 2$, and assume `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b q`: $a<0$, $b<0$, and for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ the algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$ has every nonzero element invertible exactly when $q\in w$. Let $R$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule which is an Eichler order of level $N$, i.e. $R=\Lambda_1\cap\Lambda_2$ for two maximal orders with relative index $N$, where an order is a finitely generated $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule containing $1$, closed under multiplication and spanning $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, and maximal means maximal among orders for inclusion. Let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order with $R\le\Lambda$, let $r$ be a prime with $r\neq q$, and let $v$ be a height-one prime with $r\in v$. Then there is a unit $\bar w$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w)=q$, where $\mathrm{nrd}(x)=x_{\mathrm{re}}^2-ax_I^2-bx_J^2+abx_K^2$, such that: for every $w\neq v$ with $q\notin w$, the image $\bar w\otimes 1$ in $(\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w)^\times$ lies in [`Submodule.localBoxUnits R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L45), i.e. it and its inverse lie in the additive subgroup generated by the $z\otimes c$ with $z\in R$ and $c$ in the valuation ring; and for every $w\neq v$ and every $x\in\mathbb{H}\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{Q}_w$, conjugation $x\mapsto (\bar w\otimes 1)^{-1}x(\bar w\otimes 1)$ preserves membership in [`Submodule.localBox R w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40) and in [`Submodule.localBox Λ w`](def/Submodule_LocalBox.html#L40), in both directions.
--
--   This is the global Atkin–Lehner element at the ramified prime $q$ of a definite rational quaternion algebra, normalised so as to be a local unit of $R$ at all finite places other than the chosen place $v$ above $r$ and to normalise the completions of both $R$ and $\Lambda$ there. It feeds the $r$-adic Čerednik–Drinfeld description of the Shimura curve of discriminant $qr$, being used in the construction of Shimura curve models with Hecke tower and interchange data.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraph_exists_units_nrd_eq_ramifiedPrime_forall_mem_localBoxUnits_and_normalizes.lean

